<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/10th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Srivijayan invasion of Medang</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">990 CE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Srivijayan invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medang-kingdom">Medang</a> was a military campaign by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srivijaya">Srivijaya</a> against the Javanese kingdom of Medang in 990 CE. The Srivijaya Empire profile cites it as evidence that Srivijaya could project force across considerable distances. It reflected rivalry between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumatra">Sumatra</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a>.</p></div>
